      "section": "7.2.3 RUBBER FOOT PAD REPLACEMENT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 72.0,
        "t": 738.192,
        "r": 356.77268399999986,
        "b": 709.2829284297521
      },
      "content": "7.2.3 RUBBER FOOT PAD REPLACEMENT",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0795",
      "reading_order": 867,
      "section": "7.2.3 RUBBER FOOT PAD REPLACEMENT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 72.0,
        "t": 695.1027600000001,
        "r": 504.0090239999997,
        "b": 686.2073370491804
      },
      "content": "Recommended tools for this procedure are an X-acto knife, mild solvent, and lint-free cloth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0796",
      "reading_order": 868,
      "section": "7.2.3 RUBBER FOOT PAD REPLACEMENT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 72.0,
        "t": 671.1031440000002,
        "r": 281.66397599999976,
        "b": 662.2077210491805
      },
      "content": "The replacement part for this procedure is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0797",
      "reading_order": 869,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.999712,
        "t": 653.1034320000001,
        "r": 179.53313999999986,
        "b": 644.3470000327869
      },
      "content": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0798",
      "reading_order": 870,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 72.0,
        "t": 627.1237680000002,
        "r": 417.6289320000004,
        "b": 618.2283450491805
      },
      "content": "To replace the rubber foot pad, see Figure 7-1 , then proceed as follows:",
      "hyperlink_hint": true
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0799",
      "reading_order": 871,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.58039600000001,
        "t": 603.1241520000001,
        "r": 408.2336639999995,
        "b": 594.2287290491804
      },
      "content": "Turn off the infuser and disconnect the device from AC power."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0800",
      "reading_order": 872,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.58039600000001,
        "t": 587.7040800000001,
        "r": 242.73631199999986,
        "b": 578.8086570491804
      },
      "content": "Place the infuser on its side."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0801",
      "reading_order": 873,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.58039600000001,
        "t": 572.2242480000001,
        "r": 503.9412960000003,
        "b": 551.9286090491804
      },
      "content": "Using the X-acto knife, remove the rubber foot pad and scrape the enclosure recess to remove adhesive residue."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0802",
      "reading_order": 874,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 108.0,
        "t": 548.1,
        "r": 504.0835919999998,
        "b": 519.1075290491804
      },
      "content": " Note: Each  adhesive-backed  rubber  foot  pad  is  bonded  in  its  recess. Do not damage the recess."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0803",
      "reading_order": 875,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.580264,
        "t": 508.023192,
        "r": 504.0049079999997,
        "b": 487.6677930491803
      },
      "content": "Using  mild  solvent  and  a  lint-free  cloth,  clean  any  adhesive  residue  from  the enclosure recess."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0804",
      "reading_order": 876,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.58026400000003,
        "t": 481.143144,
        "r": 503.99992799999904,
        "b": 460.78774504918033
      },
      "content": "Remove the protective backing from the self-adhesive surface of the replacement foot pad and press the pad in place."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0805",
      "reading_order": 877,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 89.57926800000004,
        "t": 454.263096,
        "r": 407.38195199999944,
        "b": 445.3676730491803
      },
      "content": "After approximately five minutes, verify the foot pad is secure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0806",
      "reading_order": 878,
      "section": "Pad, Rubber Foot",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 71.99887200000003,
        "t": 430.803312,
        "r": 503.97203999999977,
        "b": 397.9082730491803
      },
      "content": "Replacement of a rubber foot pad is routine maintenance and no verification procedure is normally required. However, if the infuser may have been damaged during rubber foot pad replacement, perform the PVT in Section 5.2 ."
    }
  ],
